<title>UK: COBHAM SQUEEZED UP IN THIN VOLUME.</title>
<headline>COBHAM SQUEEZED UP IN THIN VOLUME.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British engineering group Cobham Plc leapt up on Thursday as demand amid tight volume pushed up the price, analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is quite illiquid and not traded very much,&quot; said Barnaby Wiener, engineering analyst at Merrill Lynch. It only took a little interest to move the stock dramatically, he said.</p>
<p>By 0900 GMT the shares were ahead 33p at 806-1/2p, up over four percent on the day, with a mere 30,000 shares traded.</p>
<p>&quot;It is squeezy, people are short,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
